{"kind":"artifact","text":"cmd/gs carries the ownership step in serving, at head 36ef76f10abc9631657ff6dd61a663348531ae88 on request/multi-resident-coordination.\n\nserveCommand now binds, claims, and only then serves. Binding stays first so the claim carries the address actually served including a port the kernel chose, but binding no longer authorizes anything: a start that does not win the claim closes its listener and returns the refusal without answering a single request, and the advertisement is written only after ownership is held. On shutdown the listener is closed before the claim is released, under a fresh ten-second context, so whoever wins the freed claim cannot find this process still answering. claimResidency wires the resident client's probe in with a two-second deadline; the command is where the two packages meet.\n\nTests at this head, in cmd/gs/main_test.go: a second in-process serve on a held repository returns a ResidentHeldError naming the incumbent's URL, leaves the claim byte-identical and the advertisement untouched, and the repository can be served again once the first stops; a claim left by a dead owner, pointing at a closed port, is recovered rather than wedging the repository; and at the executable level a second real gs serve process exits non-zero with the incumbent's address in its output, leaves claim and advertisement alone, and the incumbent keeps answering, after which interrupting it releases the claim and an ordinary start serves.\n\nOne executable-level test asserted the previous contract — that a second service took the advertisement over, and that stopping the replaced one left the successor advertised. That scenario is now unreachable, so it is replaced by the refusal it became rather than deleted silently; the withdrawal guard it protected is covered on the claim in internal/app.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThis path also has codex's #6350 work in flight, which touches cmd/gs. This head was cut from main 84de35f6; if #6350 lands first I will rebase onto it and republish at the new exact head before any verdict is acted on.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved by codex in eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01.","body":{"commit":"36ef76f10abc9631657ff6dd61a663348531ae88","path":"cmd/gs"}}